<h1>Formal Objection, Demand for Review and Preservation of Records</h1>

<p><strong>To:</strong> Philip Glass, NSW Trustee &amp; Guardian<br>
<strong>From:</strong> Richard William McLean<br>
<strong>Date:</strong> 22 October 2026</p>

<div class="box">
<p><strong>Note:</strong> This page records a formal objection and requests for review. Statements about contested events, conduct, motives or responsibility are allegations or personal testimony, not established court findings.</p>
</div>

<h2>Formal objection</h2>
<p>I place before NSW Trustee &amp; Guardian my formal objection, personal testimony, documentary record and demands for accountability concerning accommodation, financial hardship, Able Point, NDIS funding, vehicle disposal, whistleblower detriment, loss of independence and institutional conduct.</p>

<p>I require a substantive written response addressing the matters below individually, rather than a general administrative reply.</p>

<h2>Accommodation and Able Point</h2>
<p>I object to any assumption that my current accommodation arrangement at Able Point should be treated as acceptable or permanent without proper examination of my wishes, circumstances, rights and available alternatives.</p>

<p>I request copies of relevant agreements, occupancy documents, service agreements, consent records, assessments, decisions and communications, to the extent permitted by law.</p>

<p>I also request a written explanation of the process available if I wish to leave, including arrangements for accommodation, belongings, finances, transport and continuity of support.</p>

<h2>Decision-making and accountability</h2>
<p>I request identification of the decisions personally made, authorised, reviewed or supervised by Philip Glass; the information available at the time; the reasoning recorded; and the division of responsibility with any other person or organisation.</p>

<h2>Vehicle decision</h2>
<p>The vehicle was connected to my independence, mobility and ability to manage daily life. I request a written explanation of the decision-making process, alternatives considered, evidence relied upon, effect on my independence, and available review mechanisms.</p>

<ul>
<li><a href="https://github.com/wezzo72/Barrandodger/blob/main/2025-11-14_NSW_Trustee_Vehicle_Disposal_Decision.pdf">Vehicle disposal decision, 14 November 2025</a></li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/wezzo72/Barrandodger/blob/main/2024-10-16_NSW_Trustee_Guardian_s122.pdf">NSW Trustee &amp; Guardian section 122 document, 16 October 2024</a></li>
</ul>

<h2>Able Point complaints</h2>
<p>I request written confirmation of the relevant management and complaint structures, the appropriate executive or manager responsible for responding to concerns, and the escalation pathway.</p>

<p>I request preservation and review of relevant case notes, incident reports, staff communications, service records, complaints, assessments and correspondence.</p>

<h2>NDIS funding and services</h2>
<p>I request a transparent account of the services funded, services recorded as delivered, service agreements, support plans, invoices, delivery records, incident reports, complaints and communications that can lawfully be provided.</p>

<p>Where a matter concerns NDIS service delivery, funding, provider conduct or plan decisions, I request identification of the relevant referral pathway, including the <a href="https://www.ndiscommission.gov.au/">NDIS Quality and Safeguards Commission</a>.</p>

<h2>Scott Treadwell correspondence</h2>
<p>I refer to correspondence attributed to Scott Treadwell dated 8 January 2024 concerning matters associated with the Federal Court. I request that it be read in full and addressed on its actual contents.</p>

<p><a href="https://github.com/wezzo72/Barrandodger/blob/main/08.01.2024%20scott%20treadwell%20Federal%20Court%20-%20superannuation%20and%20NDIS%20CEO%20copy%202.pdf">Scott Treadwell correspondence, 8 January 2024</a></p>

<p>I request confirmation whether maladministration, alleged coordination adverse to my interests, and conduct capable of causing harm were considered; what action was taken or recommended; who decided; what information was available; and why any protective or corrective action did or did not follow.</p>

<h2>Financial hardship</h2>
<p>My financial position requires urgent, transparent review. The figures previously provided were pension income of $1,371.27 per fortnight, listed outgoings of $1,369.96 per fortnight, and an apparent remaining amount of $1.31 per fortnight.</p>

<p>I request an itemised explanation of any allowance reduction, including the amount before and after, effective date, reasons, evidence considered, decision-maker and review process.</p>

<p>I also request urgent assessment of whether emergency assistance or a temporary adjustment is available for essential expenses.</p>

<h2>Bank access</h2>
<p>I allege that my access to my Commonwealth Bank account through internet banking and the mobile application has been restricted.</p>

<p>I request immediate written explanation of the legal or administrative authority relied upon, date of restriction, decision-maker, reasons, consideration of my welfare and views, emergency access arrangements, and internal and external review pathways.</p>

<h2>Preservation of records</h2>
<p>I request preservation of relevant case notes, correspondence, financial records, internal decision records, complaints and communications with service providers, subject to applicable law and retention requirements.</p>

