<h2>Formal demands</h2>
<ol>
<li>Provide accommodation agreements, consent records and decisions.</li>
<li>Identify responsible decision-makers and the scope of Philip Glass’s role.</li>
<li>Provide vehicle-decision records, reasons, alternatives and review pathways.</li>
<li>Confirm the Able Point management contact and complaint pathway.</li>
<li>Identify service agreements, support records, invoices, case notes and incident records that can lawfully be provided.</li>
<li>Address the Scott Treadwell correspondence and the three identified matters.</li>
<li>Provide an itemised explanation of the allowance reduction and assess emergency assistance.</li>
<li>Explain immediately any restriction on access to my Commonwealth Bank account.</li>
<li>Preserve relevant records subject to applicable law.</li>
<li>Confirm receipt and accessibility of all linked documents.</li>
<li>Identify appropriate referrals for matters outside NSW Trustee &amp; Guardian’s authority.</li>
<li>Provide a named contact, confirm receipt, and state when a substantive response can be expected.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Final request</h2>
<p>I ask for a human, documented and accountable response: an explanation of decisions within NSW Trustee &amp; Guardian’s authority, preservation of records, identification of correctable errors, and a clear timetable for response.</p>

<p><strong>Yours sincerely,</strong><br>
<strong>Richard William McLean</strong><br>
Barran Dodger / Baron Dodger</p>

